<br>

#### **AI 101 for Educators** is a free, introductory online learning series for teachers and educators who want to better understand artificial intelligence (AI) and its role in education. The series is designed to help educators build confidence in teaching with and about AI.

#### In this five-part series, we’ll explain key AI concepts, discuss responsible use, examine issues like bias, and share practical examples of how AI tools can support student learning.

#### **Bringing AI to the Classroom** is the fourth module in the five module series.

___

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 95%; margin: 20pt auto; padding: 0 5px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/36211eedb3698751fa5523b4dde93351-image-1760467094025.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/7f813b0aec7d472e470f94eb91471aa1-image-1760466945803.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/ddb463a06ccc88f5d7390a1f841a0f31-image-1760467013014.png" style="border-radius: 5pt; width: 32%;">
</div>

___


#### **By the end of this professional learning module, you will be able to:**

* #### Critically evaluate AI tools and resources for their applicability and effectiveness in the classroom.

* #### AI implementation strategies through the lens of Universal Design for Learning and Culturally Responsive Teaching.


* #### Explore how you could introduce and integrate AI technologies into your own classroom settings, taking into consideration your specific educational contexts and student needs.

* #### Learn about the resources available to teach about AI in your classroom.


